Tasks: `copy` (FR5, FR6), `paste` (FR7–FR11) and Sustituir `copy here` por `copy`
y `paste` en `PatternGrid` (Fase 3, pattern-copy_20260910)

Three plan tasks in one commit, deliberately: removing `copy here` and adding
`copy`/`paste` is one change of signature on `PatternGrid`, and splitting it
would leave a commit that does not compile.

**This closes the reported defect.** With the transport stopped, `copy` in one
slot and `paste` in another now change the content — which `copy here` never
did — and the clipboard holds the whole Pattern, so it crosses Banks.

- `copyPattern()` loads the current slot of the current Bank. It reads the
  material saved in the Bank and not `pattern`, the live copy, so a Temp or Ctrl
  All overlay in flight is not frozen into a slot (FR6) — the same rule
  `recordEdit()` already follows. Available stopped and running (FR5).
- `pastePattern()` writes into the Bank being looked at, whatever Bank the
  material came from (FR7). The destination comes from
  `PatternClipboard.destination(...)` (FR8). It moves no selection, arms
  nothing, touches neither the transport nor `pendingAdoption` (FR10), and
  triggers the Bank autosave (FR11).
- `copyPattern(from:to:)` is the chord's entry point: it copies and loads the
  clipboard with the origin (FR19). Nothing calls it until Fase 4.
- `copyingSelectedPattern(to:)` is now gone (FR23) — the decision Fase 1
  deferred. Its App caller was the defect. `PatternCopyTests` keeps what was
  only its own (clearing, and neither operation moving the selection) and hands
  the copy cases to `PatternCopyWithOriginTests`, which state the origin.
- `paste` is disabled while the clipboard is empty (FR4). `clear` is untouched,
  as the spec's Out of Scope asks.

